cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "CNCD: Detecting Factual Contradictions in News Based on Large Language Models"
abstract: >-
  Online news is abundant but its authenticity is often unverified. Prior work detects deliberately
  fabricated content well, yet struggles with reports not intended as fabrications but later proved
  false. This work detects factual contradictions by cross-validating reports describing the same
  event, in two steps: identifying denial reports, and locating the corresponding denied reports.
  We release CNCD (Chinese News Contradiction Dataset) with 1,957 denial reports, 800 denied reports
  and 5,022 manually verified contradictory news pairs, drawn from 105,361 public Chinese news
  articles from March to May 2023. Step 1 achieves a recall above 97%; Step 2 reaches an F1 of 62.99
  with the LLM Filter alone at 170.99 hours, and the full filter cascade trades that down to F1 36.21
  at 17.63 hours, giving an explicit accuracy-versus-compute frontier.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gninaij/CNCD"
keywords:
  - fake news detection
  - fact extraction
  - large language model
  - fact-checking
  - contradiction detection
  - Chinese NLP
authors:
